-- Safe to re-run: only updates tactical_explanations.

UPDATE public.economics_cases SET tactical_explanations = ARRAY['FALSE — The claim is false. The net change in cash and cash equivalents for a period has no relationship to the cash flows from operating, investing and financing activities.

The task tests income statement, cash flow statement, and financial statement timing. Financial statements distinguish stocks (balance sheet at a date) from flows (income and cash over a period); many false statements swap those roles.

Apply the case evidence: The net change in cash is exactly the sum of the operating, investing and financing cash flows for the period. Check whether the direction of change (higher/lower, above/below the threshold) matches what the statement asserts.

Because the decisive detail is wrong, mark the statement false.', 'FALSE — On the Fuhrmann definition used in the entrance exam, the sentence is false. When reconciling profit to cash generated from operating activities under the indirect method, depreciation charged during the year is deducted a second time from profit.

The task tests income statement, cash flow statement, and financial statement timing. Financial statements distinguish stocks (balance sheet at a date) from flows (income and cash over a period); many false statements swap those roles.

Apply the case evidence: Depreciation is added back to profit in this reconciliation, not deducted again, because it never involved a cash payment. Check whether the direction of change (higher/lower, above/below the threshold) matches what the statement asserts.

The statement sounds plausible but fails on precision, so it is false.', 'FALSE — On the Fuhrmann definition used in the entrance exam, the sentence is false. Accumulated depreciation is added to the original cost of a fixed asset to arrive at its carrying value.

The task tests income statement, cash flow statement, and financial statement timing. Financial statements distinguish stocks (balance sheet at a date) from flows (income and cash over a period); many false statements swap those roles.

Apply the case evidence: Carrying value equals cost less accumulated depreciation, not cost plus accumulated depreciation. Check whether the direction of change (higher/lower, above/below the threshold) matches what the statement asserts.

Once the overclaim or mislabel is exposed, the only consistent answer is false.', 'TRUE — On the Fuhrmann definition used in the entrance exam, the sentence is correct. When a bakery collects payment from a customer who owed money on an overdue invoice, the resulting cash inflow belongs in cash flow from operating activities.

The task tests income statement, cash flow statement, and financial statement timing. Financial statements distinguish stocks (balance sheet at a date) from flows (income and cash over a period); many false statements swap those roles.

Apply the case evidence: Collecting money owed by a customer relates to core trading activity, so it is classified as an operating cash flow. Check whether the direction of change (higher/lower, above/below the threshold) matches what the statement asserts.

Every part of the claim aligns with the standard concept, so the statement stands.', 'FALSE — On the Fuhrmann definition used in the entrance exam, the sentence is false. A rise in inventory or trade receivables during the year has no effect on cash and is fully reflected in profit for the period in exactly the same way.

The underlying topic is income statement, cash flow statement, and financial statement timing. When figures appear, the exam checks whether you can interpret them in accounting terms—what increased, what ratio is implied, and whether the label (current, non-current, equity, and so on) fits.

Apply the case evidence: Working capital increases use cash without moving through profit the same way, which is part of why profit and operating cash flow diverge. Check whether the direction of change (higher/lower, above/below the threshold) matches what the statement asserts.

Once the overclaim or mislabel is exposed, the only consistent answer is false.'] WHERE case_id = 'CASE 6.2.126' AND tier = 'full';
